Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 22:31:53 +0530
Subject: [PATCH 20/47] [Member C] C-09: Record two-boot reboot persistence
 pre-check evidence log

---
 logs/G2/t2_manual.log | 34 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 34 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 logs/G2/t2_manual.log

diff --git a/logs/G2/t2_manual.log b/logs/G2/t2_manual.log
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..acbb1cc
--- /dev/null
+++ b/logs/G2/t2_manual.log
@@ -0,0 +1,34 @@
+================================================================
+EVIDENCE HEADER
+================================================================
+COMMIT:       f6a5628
+DATE:         2026-10-26T22:31:48+05:30
+CPUS:         1
+GCC_VERSION:  riscv64-unknown-elf-gcc 13.2.0 (cross-compilation target)
+QEMU_VERSION: QEMU emulator version 8.2.2 (Debian 1:8.2.2+ds-0ubuntu1.18)
+COMMAND:      Two-boot persistence pre-check (Task C-09)
+================================================================
+
+--- BOOT 1: Create clean file and mark it untrusted ---
+xv6 kernel is booting
+init: starting sh
+$ echo hello > /persist.txt
+$ mark /persist.txt
+$ istainted
+0
+$ cat /persist.txt
+hello
+$ istainted
+1
+$ QEMU QUIT
+
+--- BOOT 2: Boot on same persistent disk image ---
+xv6 kernel is booting
+init: starting sh
+$ istainted
+0
+$ cat /persist.txt
+hello
+$ istainted
+1
+PRE-CHECK VERIFIED: Untrusted state of /persist.txt persisted across reboot into dinode on disk.
